From c8e8e754ae068115b27ff9ffc20225afa9e69470 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 03:49:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/40] verify: STRATA_BATCH_SELF_COMMIT=1 lets a
 one-row-per-slot batch window keep its rows itself

A pipelined batch window is followed on its stage's stream by the layout's commit graph, and the stage counts
as done only after both. When every row of the window is another slot's one token, that commit is
unconditional (each slot keeps its one row; commit_slot_prefixes allows nothing else), and most of the
graph only repeats what the window wrote: it puts each indexer tail back from its snapshot and appends the
same row again, and copies each PLE history back from the window's own snapshot of it. What it adds is the
GDN conv history and recurrence state, which the window ran without writing.

With the switch, such a window advances the GDN conv history (gdn_conv_l2_multi with commit) and state
(gdn_step_norm_multi with n_keep = 1, the kernel the commit graph runs for a one-row group) itself, as a
one-token solo window does, and takes no tail or history snapshots. No commit graph is captured for the
layout; batch_launch and commit_slot_prefixes launch none, layout_captured and ensure_batch_layouts do not
ask for one. Layouts with proposal rows (--batch-mtp) keep the commit graph. With the switch off every path
is unchanged.

Measured on 4x RTX 3090, UD-IQ4_XS, T16-142fcb (split 12,24,37), decode of 16 / 32 slots, 30 s each,
reference and new build back to back: 653.7 -> 686.0 rows/s (+4.9 %) and 714.1 -> 752.6 rows/s (+5.4 %);
the group step period 24.5 -> 23.3 ms and 44.85 -> 42.6 ms. STRATA_VERIFY_PROFILE: the window's GDN
recurrence takes 0.09 ms (16) / 0.18 ms (32) longer per stage-window with the state written in it.

batch_test16 (16 slots, a 1,200-token prompt) is token-identical to the reference dump; batch_test32
32/32 identical and its dump equal to the switch-off run; batch_overlap_test (STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP=1) passes
and is token- and RESUME-identical to the switch-off run; batch_interleave_test parts 1-3 identical (its
part 4 fails at the same point with the reference build).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
